### Request
GET /api/v1/hello?extra=param HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:19320

### Response (captured 2026-07-31)
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Content-Length: 33
Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 13:58:24 GMT
Server: Kestrel

{"message":"Hello from Baseerah"}

### Observation
An undeclared query string appended to a declared route is silently ignored; the endpoint still
returns its normal 200 greeting. Correct and intended (the contract declares no query
parameters for this operation), but uncovered by existing Gherkin -- `greeting.feature`'s
scenario only issues a bare `GET /api/v1/hello`. Proposed as SG-004.
